andy: Pushed PR #7123 to refresh the Vercel quickstart (hello-vercel). Main fixes: use REDWOOD_API_KEY from env, call out Vercel dashboard env var path, and remove streaming example which doesn't work in serverless functions.

mina: Can you paste the serverless function snippet so I can check the env usage?

andy: Sure — Node 18, Serverless Function (api/hello.js):

```js
export default async function handler(req, res) {
  const API_KEY = process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY
  if (!API_KEY) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'missing REDWOOD_API_KEY' })
  const body = { input: req.body?.text || '' }
  const r = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${API_KEY}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify(body)
  })
  const data = await r.json()
  res.status(200).json(data)
}
```

sergio: tiny nit: mention that Vercel env vars are set in Project Settings -> Environment Variables and that Preview vs Production scopes are separate.

mina: Also add a one-line migration note for SDK v6: if folks used the Vercel runtime helper, switch to reading REDWOOD_API_KEY from env and use the new client constructor (link to migration guide).

andy: Will add the dashboard path, the migration blurb, and a troubleshooting line about 401s in Preview when env is only set for Production.

